This form of any vector is called its \textit{component form}. Here, $x$, $y$ and $z$ are called
as the \textit{scalar components} of $\vec{r}$, and $x\hat{i}$, $y\hat{j}$ and $z\hat{k}$ are called the \textit{vector components}
of $\vec{r}$ along the respective axes. Sometimes $x$, $y$ and $z$ are also termed as \textit{rectangular}
\textit{components}.
